lines=['# perf12 — batch 60 performance vs live batch 59','',f"**{'PASS'if allpass else'perf pending'}: {passed(m['matrix'])}/15 original matrix cells, {passed(m['moments'])}/9 event windows, {passed(x)}/9 added native route cells.**",'','The orchestrator ended the quiet-window wait because PO testing and seven concurrent lanes will keep the Mac busy for the next hours. All completed measurements pass. Eight added route cells and the complete-frame SSR cost diagnostic remain **perf pending**.','',f"Fresh public candidate source `{p['revision']}`, bundle `{p['candidateBundle']}`, SHA-256 `{p['candidateBundleSha256']}`. Control: live PROD batch 59 mirror, bundle `{p['prodBundle']}`, SHA-256 `{p['prodBundleSha256']}`.",'','## Verdict table','','Loads are cold/warm seconds. Frame values are milliseconds, PROD → candidate.','', '| Scope | Cell / moment | PROD cold / warm s | Candidate cold / warm s | p95 ms P → C | Max ms P → C | Verdict |','|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|']
for r in m['matrix']:
 load=lambda side:' / '.join(f"{r['loads'][side][t]/1000:.3f}"for t in['cold','warm'])
 native=r['native'];pair=lambda k:' → '.join(f(native[s][k])for s in['prod','candidate'])if native else'—'
 lines.append(f"| {r['backend']} | {r['level']} {r['tier']} | {load('prod')} | {load('candidate')} | {pair('p95')} | {pair('maximum')} | {r['verdict']} |")
for r in m['moments']:
 pair=lambda k:' → '.join(f(r['sides'][s][k])for s in['prod','candidate'])
 lines.append(f"| Moment | {r['level']} {r['name']} {r['tier']} | — | — | {pair('p95')} | {pair('maximum')} | {r['verdict']} |")
lines+=['','## Added route coverage','','| Native minute | Tier | p95 ms P → C | Max ms P → C | Sampled path m P → C | Verdict |','|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---|']
labels={'r4':'L10 R4 military crossing','r6':'L10 R6 southern forecourt','approach':'L10 complex approach','drive':'L9 open drive','wet':'Wet L1 / SSR active'}
for r in x:
 pair=lambda k:' → '.join(f(r['sides'][s][k])if s in r['sides']else'—'for s in['prod','candidate'])
 travel=' → '.join(f(r['coverage'][s]['sampledPathM'])if s in r['coverage']else'—'for s in['prod','candidate'])
 lines.append(f"| {labels[r['slice']]} | {r['tier']} | {pair('p95')} | {pair('maximum')} | {travel} | {r['verdict']} |")
lines+=['','## Causes and fixes','']
if(O/'attribution12.json').exists():
 a=read('attribution12.json');lines+=[item for paragraph in a['reportParagraphs']for item in [paragraph,'']]
elif p['sourceFixCommits']:
 lines+=['Source changes exist; causal evidence is not yet packaged.']
else:lines+=['No runtime source change is credited.']
if(O/'ssr-cost.json').exists():
 d=read('ssr-cost.json');lines+=['','### SSR complete-frame cost — perf pending','',d['method'].rstrip('.')+'.','']
 for row in d['rows']:
  for g in row['groups']:
   values=[s['frameTimelineMs']for s in g['samples']if s.get('frameTimelineMs')is not None]
   if values:lines.append(f"- SSR {'on'if g['ssrEnabled']else'off'}: mean complete GPU timeline bracket {statistics.mean(values):.3f} ms, {len(values)} samples.")
  if not all('frameTimelineMs'in s for g in row['groups']for s in g['samples']):
   lines.append('Complete-frame SSR cost diagnostic remains unmeasured. Nested pass sums overlap and do not supply a whole-frame cost.');continue
  on=[s['frameTimelineMs']for g in row['groups']if g['ssrEnabled']for s in g['samples']];off=[s['frameTimelineMs']for g in row['groups']if not g['ssrEnabled']for s in g['samples']]
  lines.append(f"- Pooled on minus off: {statistics.mean(on)-statistics.mean(off):+.3f} ms per serialized frame bracket. This includes CPU submission gaps and is diagnostic cost attribution; the separate native wet minute supplies the performance verdict.")
lines+=['','## Method and limits','',f"{p['toolchain']['cpu']} / macOS {p['toolchain']['macOS']} ({p['toolchain']['macOSBuild']}), Chromium {p['toolchain']['chromium']} / Playwright {p['toolchain']['playwright']}. Headless native Metal WebGPU and ANGLE Metal WebGL2, 1280×720, DPR 1, seed 1. Timing commands enter through `tools/perf/quiet-run.sh`, with exclusive browser admission, host load below 3 at admission, no busy foreign work and one context at a time.",'','The first added-route reservation expired at the 600 s cap during host preflight while foreign r12 checks were active. No timing child or capture started. The terminal command receipt and wait conditions are retained. The retry waited outside reservations and was stopped by the orchestrator before admission.','', 'Cold means an isolated context; warm is its reload. GPU/driver caches remain shared; the link census supplies the causal evidence. Original public menu bytes measure level-button click to loading-card closure. G-01 checks Begin mission on L1 low WebGL2 cold. Gameplay exposes only the existing Game instance at bootstrap and uses the same current-source test adapter on both public bundles. Each side retains its own native simulation, rendering and content. CPU-profiled diagnostics never supply a verdict. A read-only long-task observer is installed on both sides.','', 'All original WebGPU cells cover at least 60 seconds of native gameplay; both L1 tiers and L10 high cover at least 90 seconds. The complete bot supplies ordinary InputFrames, with courier survival protection. L1 withholds terminal exit movement to retain the level. L7 pickup/rocket and L10 charge run natively. The unexecuted L10 harness is prepared to walk the authored route to each checkpoint, then supply ordinary movement frames along the crossing lines with native combat. The unexecuted L9 harness is prepared to use ordinary steering/throttle on the open route. The wet L1 high scene runs native rain/weather after 4,000 preparation ticks, with SSR active for the candidate minute.','', 'L1 handover/outbreak ends two seconds after infected exit. L7 pickup runs from 100 ms before collection to 250 ms after; first rocket runs from 100 ms before firing through 250 ms after native impact; the combined window spans both. L10 charge includes first completion plus two seconds. Every full frame interval overlapping each window is included.','', 'Unchanged rules: candidate cold and warm each ≤6 s and ≤PROD+0.5 s; p95 ≤PROD+1 ms; max ≤PROD+one 60 Hz frame (16.7 ms plus 0.1 ms quantization tolerance). A new ≥66 ms maximum fails when PROD is below 66 ms. Inherited hitches remain visible. Single paired captures describe these routes and hardware, and do not certify all devices or routes.','', '## Validation and evidence','']
