nodes={n['id']:n for n in profile['nodes']};parent={c:n['id']for n in profile['nodes']for c in n.get('children',[])};clock=profile['performanceStartedAt'];stacks=collections.Counter();selfMs=0
for sample,dt in zip(profile['samples'],profile['timeDeltas']):
 clock+=dt/1000
 if not(r['start']<=clock<=r['done'])or nodes[sample]['callFrame']['functionName']!='getProgramParameter':continue
 selfMs+=dt/1000;stack=[]
 while sample in nodes:
  f=nodes[sample]['callFrame'];stack.append((f['functionName'],f['url'].split('/')[-1],f['lineNumber'],f['columnNumber']));sample=parent.get(sample)
 stacks[tuple(stack)]+=dt/1000
initial=[dict(r,rawSource=str(p),rawSha256=sha(p))for p in sorted((R/'initial').glob('*/loads/*.json'))for r in read(p)]
failures=[dict(level=r['level'],tier=r['tier'],backend=r['backend'],temperature=r['temperature'],candidateMs=r['ms'],prodMs=next(p['ms']for p in initial if(p['side'],p['level'],p['tier'],p['backend'],p['temperature'])==('prod',r['level'],r['tier'],r['backend'],r['temperature'])),rawSource=r['rawSource'],rawSha256=r['rawSha256'])for r in initial if r['side']=='candidate'and r['ms']>6000]
commit=subprocess.check_output(['git','rev-parse','HEAD'],text=True).strip();equiv=read(R/'source-equivalence.json')
paragraphs=[f"The initial public load sweep on `f3e603fb` fails four absolute limits: L7 high WebGPU cold **6.657 s**, and low WebGL2 L1/L4/L7 cold **7.460 / 6.028 / 9.110 s**. PROD is slower in every one of those cells; inherited cost does not waive the candidate’s 6 s limit. The twelve completed initial near-scene captures are retained; the next heavy-scene admission was deliberately stopped before a capture began to validate the repair with a complete final matrix.",f"The separate L1 cold CPU profile reproduces **6.586 s** and attributes **{selfMs:.1f} ms** of sampled time to `getProgramParameter`, including **{stacks.most_common(1)[0][1]:.1f} ms** through the nested transparent draw. Pipeline attribution identifies first-use post-processing programs and actual pet/character surfaces outside the earlier scene compilation. These diagnostics locate work; none supplies a verdict.","The repair discovers cold pipelines in the real warm-up render contexts, queues their native links asynchronously, then replays the complete draws after linking. The final foreground readiness draw does the same for surfaces exposed by unfreezing. Scene geometry, every warm-up variant and both instancing paths remain present. Gameplay restores the original backend methods. This changes loading preparation; no model, population, effects, quality tier or acceptance limit is reduced.",f"One cause commit: `{commit[:8]}` — Prepare cold warm-up pipelines before their first real draw. Focused WebGL2 cold diagnostics move synchronous links **14→2 (L1), 10→5 (L4), 13→8 (L7)** while conserving total linked programs **107 / 118 / 105** on both sides. All **{equiv['beforeAssetPaths']:,} asset-version paths** are unchanged. Shared GPU contract checks cover waiting, complete replay, frame renewal and hook restoration. The residual synchronous programs are reported; no claim of zero cold shader work is made.","An earlier material-state prototype hit an uninitialized framebuffer-copy error; its revision was discarded. A corrected version of that prototype added unused preparation without reducing the synchronous link count and was also discarded. Only the direct warm-up draw repair above is committed. Failed and diagnostic attempts remain identified in the command ledger."]
